# A picture's own styles, painted — buri-lang/buri#123. `image` was the one
# constructor with no `[Style]` slot, so a picture painted at its intrinsic size
# wherever the flow put it and an avatar could not be built.
#
# Three pictures, each a labelled grid — a claim is a band and its values read
# across. The bands are a fixed height and clip, so a cell that grows stays in
# its own row instead of squashing the ones under it.
#
# What the pictures say, and what was read in them:
#
#   * `image-size` — a picture takes `Width`, `Height`, `AspectRatio` and the
#     four bounds from its own styles. Every length CSS accepts is a size: the
#     pixel, the rem at sixteen to one, the percentage of the containing box,
#     and `Full`. `Auto` and no declaration at all are the same picture, which
#     is what a browser does with them. Two `Width`s are last-wins, which is
#     the conflict slot the property already had.
#   * `image-chrome` — the corner, the frame and the wash. A `Radius` clips the
#     picture rather than the box around it, which is the whole of what
#     `rounded-[inherit]` does in the library this was ported from; a border is
#     drawn round the corner it goes round, and the picture is drawn inside it.
#     A `BorderEdge` puts a rule under a picture with nothing else round it.
#   * `image-avatar` — the avatar the slot was asked for, and the two things a
#     program could ask for before it. The `filled` cells are the picture
#     filling a round box, cropped square and taking the corner: a real avatar.
#     The band above them is the same picture with no box at all, so what the
#     corner and the crop do is read on the picture itself.
#     `box only` is the workaround — a round box with a picture of its own size
#     inside it, square-cornered, because nothing in `ui/style` clips overflow
#     (filed separately). `no box` is the picture with nothing said to it at
#     all, which is what `image` used to be.
#
# The source is one the painter cannot load, so every cell is the placeholder
# box. That is deliberate: a snapshot fetches nothing, and the placeholder is
# painted at exactly the size and shape the styles asked for, which is the
# thing under test.
#
# The lifecycle is `sweep_properties_*`'s: every golden compares, a renamed
# snapshot is reported as missing rather than as a difference, `--update`
# records it, the run after that compares against what it wrote, and an edit to
# one number fails the comparison. Only the first run paints the whole suite;
# the ones after it are `--filter`ed to the one picture they are about.
#
# Schema: the repository-case manifest, cli/tests/harness/case.rs.

doc: "a picture sized, shaped and cropped by its own styles, and the avatar that needed all three, as 3 pictures with the whole record-and-fail lifecycle over them"

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/sweep", "--force"]
  exit: 0
  golden: "pass.txt"
}

path { path: "lib/sweep/test/__snapshots__/image-size.diff.png"  exists: false }

# A snapshot nobody has recorded yet is reported as missing, with the command
# that records one, rather than as a difference against nothing.
edit {
  file: "lib/sweep/test/pictures.buri"
  replace: "\"image-size\""
  with: "\"never-recorded\""
}

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/sweep", "--force", "--filter=sized"]
  exit: 1
  golden: "missing.txt"
}

path { path: "lib/sweep/test/__snapshots__/never-recorded.png"  exists: false }

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/sweep", "--update", "--force", "--filter=sized"]
  exit: 0
  golden: "recorded.txt"
}

path { path: "lib/sweep/test/__snapshots__/never-recorded.png"  exists: true }

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/sweep", "--force", "--filter=sized"]
  exit: 0
  golden: "again.txt"
}

# The negative twin: four pixels on the corner of one avatar, which is the
# smallest edit that has to fail.
edit {
  file: "lib/sweep/scenes.buri"
  replace: ".Radius(.Px(10))"
  with: ".Radius(.Px(14))"
}

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/sweep", "--force", "--filter=avatar"]
  exit: 1
  golden: "changed.txt"
}

path { path: "lib/sweep/test/__snapshots__/image-avatar.diff.png"  exists: true }
